      "id": 1,
      "text": "Pomona was founded in 1869, named after the Roman goddess of fruit trees, reflecting early settlers' hopes for orchards.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pomona_kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "John Whetstone, dubbed the Apple King, founded the Pomona Fruit Company in 1898 and planted over 30,000 fruit trees.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pomona_kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Santa Fe Railroad reached Pomona in 1904, and electric lights lit the town by 1914.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pomona_kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pomona’s proximity to the Marais des Cygnes River shapes local drainage and keeps surrounding soils moist.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pomona_kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Pomona’s first post office opened in May 1870, a key step in its early community development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
